# Kobi Project Context

- These rules are review infrastructure only; they summarize existing project guidance and must not expand MVP scope.
- Treat `AGENTS.md` as the portable agent guide and keep this rule aligned with it.
- Use `README.md`, `docs/product-spec.md`, and `docs/contracts.md` as source-of-truth documents before changing behavior, architecture, or data shapes.
- Kobi v0 follows the loop: Listen -> Understand -> Propose -> Approve -> Deliver -> Measure.
- Preserve the TypeScript monorepo shape: `apps/web`, `apps/worker`, and shared packages under `packages/*`.
- Do not introduce Python, FastAPI, or a second backend stack unless the product spec changes.
- Keep changes scoped to the app or package that owns the behavior.
- Treat `prompts/` as runtime-tunable prompt and rubric content, not application code.
- Run the narrowest relevant validation for changed files, and state clearly when no real check exists yet.
